{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Pharaoh's chariots and his army He cast into the sea.</b> The matter requires explanation: why, regarding Pharaoh and his army that were close to him, did he say ״יָרָה בַיָּם״, and regarding his chosen officers he said ״טֻבְּעוּ בְיַם סוּף״ (Exodus 15:4)? And it appears possible to explain that since Pharaoh advanced himself and went ahead of all his forces, accordingly, when Pharaoh was together with his army that were close to his chariot within the sea itself — that is, in its middle part, where there is no reed and bulrush — his servants and chosen officers were still near the edge of the sea, a place where reeds and bulrushes grow, and also mire and mud are found there. And there they sank in the mud of the depth that is found in the place where the reeds grow, for the waters are not so deep there. And at that same time Pharaoh was in the sea itself, and there the term sinking is not applicable, for there is no mud and mire there. And a proof for this is what Rashi explained: one verse says ״רָמָה בַיָּם״ and one says ״יָרָה בַיָּם״ — this teaches that they would rise upward and sink to the abyss, etc.; and this is possible only in a place where the waters are deep, and there is no place for reed and bulrush there, as is known."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:20:18.660128790Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}